  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1225 PM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nTemperatures will remain in the high 60s throughout the whole CWA\ntoday and tomorrow and raise to the mid 70s Wednesday and\nthroughout the week. Dry air following the front will keep\nprecipitable water vaules around normal to below normal, a low\n(20%) chance Wednesday and Thursday. Winds inland are expected to\nlower through the day, and stay from the north-east at 5-10 mph\nand returning to normal onshore flow towards the end of the week.\nClouds are expected to clear overnight tonight and return\nWednesday morning. \n\nConditions are still favorable for minor coastal flooding and high\nrip current risk as longer swell periods of 7-9 seconds and\nnortheasterly flow remain.",
